<title>GERMANY: German May 1997 metals output detailed.</title>
<headline>German May 1997 metals output detailed.</headline>
<dateline>ESCHBORN, Germany 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>German copper and lead output rose in Jan/May 1997 while zinc and aluminium output were lower than in the same 1996 period, official figures showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Base metals data from the state statistics office Bundesamt fuer Wirtschaft (BAW) also showed output of semi-finished non-ferrous metals products in the five months was higher than a year earlier.</p>
<p>But the rate of increase over the same 1996 period in Jan/May had fallen versus Jan/April in all semis except nickel.</p>
<p>Castings figures were higher than a year earlier, with the exception of lead and tin.</p>
<p>The report gave the following details, in tonnes --</p>
<p>METALS OUTPUT	    May 97  Jan/May 97 Cumulative pct change</p>
<p>								over Jan/May 96</p>
<p>primary aluminium	48,256  235,203		  -  2.4</p>
<p>electrolytic copper    50,936  248,151		  +  1.1</p>
<p>zinc			 27,516  131,551		  -  3.4</p>
<p>refined lead	     23,715  100,133		  + 31.0</p>
<p>SEMI-FINISHED MTLS     May 97  Jan/May 97 Pct change over 1996</p>
<p>aluminium		 136,833  715,386		  + 17.3</p>
<p>copper		    123,764  660,817		  + 10.1</p>
<p>zinc			 13,496   70,855		  +  8.4</p>
<p>lead			  3,874   20,231		  + 15.1</p>
<p>nickel			1,710    8,736		  + 15.8</p>
<p>METALS CASTINGS	  May 97  Jan/May 97 Pct change over 1996</p>
<p>aluminium		  40,790  221,188		  +  5.6</p>
<p>copper			5,607   32,348		  +  4.2</p>
<p>zinc			  4,984   27,106		  +  0.7</p>
<p>lead			    286    2,240		  - 21.0</p>
<p>tin				22	 87		  -  3.3</p>
<p>Semis and castings figures included alloys. Nickel castings data were not given.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
